Bugfix: Resolve file cache entries without mimetype without a lookup

The file cache stores an unknown mimetype as -1, and the mimetype part of such
an entry is 0 when it is inserted. No mimetype has an id below 1, but the
mimetype loader still asked the memory cache and the database for these ids on
every call. A folder listing therefore cost two memory cache reads and two
database queries per entry without mimetype. Ids below 1 now resolve to no
mimetype right away.
